dma: no proactive supply for host transfers, and honour a DE re-arm

Two fixes to DMA lifecycle. A DSP-to-host channel must not be supplied
proactively: the host paces it by reading, and supplying ahead parks a word in
the transmit latch between transfers, where the next reader mistakes it for
fresh data. And a DCR write with DE=1 while a self-clearing window is still open
is a re-arm, not a no-op, so the channel must renew instead of stalling.

